WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:07.269
Before building AI adoption roadmap, define the problem and the decision it will support.

2
00:00:07.269 --> 00:00:12.544
Make the expected outcome measurable, and record what is still an assumption.

3
00:00:12.944 --> 00:00:16.531
Use Claude to challenge the proposed operating model.

4
00:00:16.531 --> 00:00:20.593
Separate assistive tasks from decisions that need approval.

5
00:00:20.593 --> 00:00:25.872
In Miro, map the owner, the evidence, and the handoff before choosing a tool.

6
00:00:26.272 --> 00:00:29.035
Turn that map into a delivery backlog.

7
00:00:29.035 --> 00:00:34.778
Record acceptance criteria, access requirements, and a stop condition in Jira.

8
00:00:34.778 --> 00:00:39.795
Compare cost and expected value in Excel before expanding the pilot.

9
00:00:40.195 --> 00:00:44.322
Bring the evidence, cost, and next decision into decision brief.

10
00:00:44.322 --> 00:00:49.158
The output is a shared direction, with clear ownership and a review point.
